 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "A type node is either a primitive string (\"int\", \"char\" or \"float\"), a generic string (\"T\" followed by one digit) or a tuple, written as a non-empty JSON list of type nodes (tuples nest, at most 20 levels). Formatting: a primitive or generic prints as itself; a tuple prints as \"[\" + its element strings joined by \", \" + \"]\"; a function type prints as \"(\" + the parameter strings joined by \", \" + \") -> \" + the return string. Level 1: given params (a list of zero or more type nodes) and returnType (a type node), return the formatted function type string.",
